        "Degree Bounds for Generic Initial Ideals of Arrangements / OWR-4990374-004 (30004601)",
        "",
        "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23395703",
        "A seven-hyperplane counterexample to a generic-initial degree bound (PR195). Over characteristic zero, Q=xy(x-y)(x-2y)zw(x+z+w) has ambient-Jacobian revlex-gin second-variable cutoff8 and a degree7 minimal generator involving the third variable. Self-contained open-set proof refutes the general-dimensional conjecture; prior three-variable arrangement theorem respected. Classical parallel connection and proof tools credited; applicable Migliore\u2013Nagel result concerns a distinct unmixed ideal. Bounded36-source/120-query audit and19 exact earlier-example comparisons; historical priority/independence unestablished, Ilardi2018 full-text access gap explicit. Two successive NEW whole-package adversaries clean (v1, then entire final v2); same paper/PDF. Extensive AI; unrefereed; no conventional human peer review."
      ],
